00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 28, 2009\r\rMayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in the Closed Session Conference Room, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Personnel Matter, pursuant to Government Code, Section 54957:\r PUBLIC EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION, Title: City Manager.\r2. Conference with Labor Negotiator, pursuant to Government Code, Section 54957.6:\r City Negotiator: City Attorney Michael G. Colantuono.\r Unrepresented Employee: \r Position or Title of Unrepresented Employee who is subject of Negotiation: City Manager.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:15 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 7:30 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Rubin Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Red Godfrey.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that there was no reportable action in closed session.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Mayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded Councilmember Groveman, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rCouncilmember Washburn presented certificates to the �Calabasas Raiders Midget Black� football team in recognition of their advancement to the Pacific Youth Football League Super Bowl. Mayor Maurer presented a proclamation to Fire Captain Jim Jordan in recognition of his retirement. Mayor Maurer presented awards to Luisa Barancik, Dr. Gary Lysik, Carmen Pressler, Monica Shinder for 5 years of service and to Arvin Petros for 10 years of service to the City. Mayor Maurer presented a plaque to Red Godfrey in recognition of her service on the Traffic & Transportation Commission. Mayor Maurer introduced Jamie Alcroft, Las Virgenes Educational Foundation, who spoke regarding an upcoming fundraising event that will be held in coordination with the Artists for the Arts.\r\r\r\r\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Martin Glatt, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the utility users tax that is imposed on residents of the City. Michael Pizsker, Calabasas, requested that the City Council place an item on the agenda regarding water conservation efforts, specifically gray water systems.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the January 14, 2009 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to authorize the purchase of the West Valley YMCA Portable Classroom at Lupin Hill Elementary School in the amount of $72,000. \r\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2009-252, requiring the removal of animal waste from public and private properties. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, and 3. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1168, approving File No. 080000979, a site plan review (PL0802184) to reduce the number of code required parking spaces from 302 to 287 and to expand the subterranean parking garage by 3,527 square feet in order to accommodate seven (7) additional parking spaces (309 parking spaces will be provided on the subject site) and a community room area for the Village at Calabasas, a recently approved mixed use project located at 23500 Park Sorrento. The modified site plan also includes six (6) additional surface level parking spaces required as a condition of the previous approval. \r\r Mayor Maurer opened the public hearing.\r\rGlenn Michitsch, Senior Planner, and Michael Klein, Associate Planner, provided the staff report.\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\r Mayor Maurer closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1168, approving File No. 080000979. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Approval of cart collection services franchise agreement with Waste Management, Inc. \r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rMartin Glatt, Calabasas, spoke regarding the proposed agreement with regards to cart replacement.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve the cart collection services franchise agreement. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1167, prohibiting the parking of truck tractors and trailers on City streets.\r\rMayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1167, prohibiting the parking of truck tractors and trailers on City streets. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2009-256, regarding graffiti abatement on private property.\r\rThe City Council concurred to continue the item to an upcoming meeting.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of January 7, 2009 to January 15, 2009. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles spoke regarding a public safety update that will be presented at the February 11, 2009 City Council meeting.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r There were no future agenda items.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN \r\rThe City Council adjourned at 9:00 p.m. to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, February 11, 2009 at 7:30 P.M. \r\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r01/28/09\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000r\b\u0000\u0000}\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u001a